    // The owner's O-385 (a) (PLAN G492-a (ii), revision 4): an Origin's slot-or-value reading is made once, by its producer at its use, and
    // a store keeps it: the local-region graph's readers take a parent as stored (its receivers resolved), the pending list reads a row
    // through its reading, and a record's Supplier takes a supplied end's operands as held. So a comparison's bound on x's region reaches a
    // nested signature or body that names the region (BU-28, BU-127) as the comparison read it: sib1, sib2, sib2c, csib2 and sib2n (two
    // Closures down) are rejected as their `var` twins (they were accepted when the graph read the stored slot back as its value); cenv, a
    // comparison in a Closure on an environment Borrow, is accepted as its twin; sib2esc and cenvg keep their twins' independent records
    // (SPEC 23.1.2). A read of x at a use in its own body still takes the value (sibr, veqzrc, cveqz; O-375 Q1 (a)); one step and no second
    // bound (sib3, sib2ok, mxy) and an initializer alias over a compared region (s6a) are as before.
